<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n32481" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">olfactus</span></b> , ūs, m.
		olfacio. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i>a smelling</i>, <i>smell</i> (post-Aug.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">thymi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					21, 21, 89, § 156</span></i>
			 (al. olfacto thymo); 32, 3, 13, § 28; 35, 15, 51,
			§ 182.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>the sense of
			smell</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">delphini nec olfactūs vestigia
					habent,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					11, 37, 50, § 137</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">10, 70, 90,
				§ 194</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
